From 121120d3e64e8a68255c475baa170f03673adff0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:47:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Add the frontend for the scanner portal,
 SelectScanners and ListScanners

This commit adds org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner with the two methods
that decide which scanners an application may use, and the backend
interface org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Scanner that draws the dialog.

SelectScanners asks the backend to show a dialog listing the scanners
the host has that match required_capabilities, and records the user's
choice as a grant for that application. ListScanners returns the
granted scanners that exist at that moment. An application never sees a
scanner it was not granted, and the frontend only grants ids it offered
to the dialog, and at most one unless multiple was asked for, so a
backend can draw the dialog but cannot widen what an application uses.

Grants are kept in memory on the application's XdpAppInfo, so they end
when the application leaves the bus. Nothing is stored in the
permission store; see the open questions in the proposal.

The scanners come from a stand-in until the helper that asks libsane
exists: with XDG_DESKTOP_PORTAL_SCANNER_FAKE=1 the portal offers two
made-up scanners, and without it there are none. The other methods of
the interface are declared and not yet implemented.

Tested on a private bus with this frontend and the xdg-desktop-portal-
gnome scanner dialog, driven by a small client: select, cancel with
Escape, multiple, required_capabilities, and a second connection that
sees no grants. Not tested: an application leaving the bus, a backend
that answers with ids it was not offered, and the permission checks of
a sandboxed caller.
